[536.534663, "i", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\n## Statute\n\n**§1. Tax imposed** (lines 1-17)\n\n(a) Married individuals filing joint returns and surviving spouses\n\nThere is hereby imposed on the taxable income of-\n\n    (1) every married individual (as defined in section 7703) who makes a single return jointly with his spouse, and\n\n    (2) every surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\n\na tax determined in accordance with the following:\n\n    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $36,900;\n    (ii) $5,535, plus 28% of the excess over $36,900 if the taxable income is over $36,900 but not over $89,150;\n    (iii) $20,165, plus 31% of the excess over $89,150 if the taxable income is over $89,150 but not over $140,000;\n    (iv) $35,928.50, plus 36% of the excess over $140,000 if the taxable income is over $140,000 but not over $250,000;\n    (v) $75,528.50, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000.\n\n**§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions** (lines 5"]
[536.534736, "i", "7-94)\n\n(d) Exemption amount\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\n\n    (3) Phaseout\n\n        (A) In general\n\n        In the case of any taxpayer whose adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b), the exemption amount shall be reduced by the applicable percentage.\n\n        (B) Applicable percentage\n\n        For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term \"applicable percentage\" means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting \"$1,250\" for \"$2,500\". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.\n\n**§152. Standard deduction** (lines 372-388)\n\n(c) Standard deduction\n\nFor purposes of this subtitle-\n\n    (2) Bas"]
[536.534768, "i", "ic standard deduction\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\n\n        (A) 200 percent of the dollar amount in effect under subparagraph (C) for the taxable year in the case of-\n\n            (i) a joint return, or\n\n            (ii) a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\n\n        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\n\n        (C) $3,000 in any other case.\n\n**§68. Overall limitation on itemized deductions** (lines 475-494)\n\n(b) Applicable amount\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    For purposes of this section, the term \"applicable amount\" means-\n\n        (A) $300,000 in the case of a joint return or a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\n\n## Reasoning\n\n**Step 1: Determine filing status**\nAlice files a joint return with her spouse. Per §1(a), the tax brackets for \"Married individuals filing joint returns\" apply.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate standard deduction**\nPer §152(c)(2)(A), the basic standard deduction for a joint return is 200% of t"]
[536.534774, "i", "he amount in §152(c)(2)(C), which is $3,000.\nStandard deduction = 200% × $3,000 = $6,000\n\n**Step 3: Calculate exemption phaseout**\nPer §151(d)(1), the exemption amount is $2,000 per exemption.\nAlice and spouse each get one exemption: 2 × $2,000 = $4,000\n\nPer §151(d)(3)(A) and §68(b)(A), the applicable amount for joint returns is $300,000.\nAlice's gross income is $684,642.\n\nExcess AGI = $684,642 - $300,000 = $384,642\n\nPer §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage is 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof).\nNumber of $2,500 fractions = ceiling($384,642 / $2,500) = ceiling(153.8568) = 154\nApplicable percentage = 154 × 2% = 308%\n\nPer §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage cannot exceed 100%.\nTherefore, exemption amount = $4,000 × 100% = $0 (fully phased out)\n\n**Step 4: Calculate taxable income**\nTaxable income = Gross income - Standard deduction - Exemptions\nTaxable income = $684,642 - $6,000 - $0 = $678,642\n\n**Step 5: Calculate tax**\nPer §1(a)(v), since taxable income ($678,642) is "]
[536.534786, "i", "over $250,000:\nTax = $75,528.50 + 39.6% × ($678,642 - $250,000)\nTax = $75,528.50 + 0.396 × $428,642\nTax = $75,528.50 + $169,742.23\nTax = $245,270.73\n\nRounded to the nearest dollar: $245,271\n\nThe agricultural labor information (employees Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George) is not relevant to Alice's personal income tax calculation under these statutes.\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 245271\nEOF\n"]
[536.534802, "o", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'"]
[536.53509, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.535099, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ## Statute\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r8\u001b[?2004h> **§1. Tax imposed** (lines 1-17)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r+\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.53516, "o", "(a) Married individuals filing joint returns and surviving spouses\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.535167, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[536.535258, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.535269, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rc\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.53543, "o", "    (1) every married individual (as defined in section 7703) who makes a single return jointly with his spouse, and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.535593, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     (2) every surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r5"]
[536.535634, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.535679, "o", "a tax determined in accordance with the following:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.535857, "o", "    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $36,900;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     (ii) $5,535, plus 28% of the excess over $36,900 if the taxable income is over $36,900 but not over $89,150;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.536066, "o", "    (iii) $20,165, plus 31% of the excess over $89,150 if the taxable income is over $89,150 but not over $140,000;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     (iv) $35,928.50, plus 36% of the excess over $140,000 if the taxable income is over $140,000 but not over $250,000;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.536237, "o", "    (v) $75,528.50, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> **§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions** (lines 57-94)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (d) Exemption amount\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.536353, "o", "    (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.536367, "o", "    (3) Phaseout\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.536372, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.536383, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.536482, "o", "        (A) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.536595, "o", "        In the case of any taxpayer whose adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b), the exemption amount shall be reduced by the applicable percentage.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.536609, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.536763, "o", "        (B) Applicable percentage\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537069, "o", "        For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term \"applicable percentage\" means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting \"$1,250\" for \"$2,500\". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537141, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> **§152. Standard deduction** (lines 372-388)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (c) Standard deduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.537171, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537197, "o", "For purposes of this subtitle-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.537226, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537254, "o", "    (2) Basic standard deduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537302, "o", "    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537337, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537407, "o", "        (A) 200 percent of the dollar amount in effect under subparagraph (C) for the taxable year in the case of-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.537442, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537464, "o", "            (i) a joint return, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.537488, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537517, "o", "            (ii) a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537539, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537568, "o", "> "]
[536.53762, "o", "        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537651, "o", "        (C) $3,000 in any other case.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537683, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537712, "o", "> "]
[536.537744, "o", "**§68. Overall limitation on itemized deductions** (lines 475-494)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.537769, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> (b) Applicable amount\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.537795, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537826, "o", "    (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537858, "o", "> "]
[536.537885, "o", "    For purposes of this section, the term \"applicable amount\" means-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.53793, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.537968, "o", "        (A) $300,000 in the case of a joint return or a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.537994, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538016, "o", "> ## Reasoning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.538054, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.538105, "o", "**Step 1: Determine filing status**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538133, "o", "> "]
[536.538211, "o", "Alice files a joint return with her spouse. Per §1(a), the tax brackets for \"Married individuals filing joint returns\" apply.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538235, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538276, "o", "> "]
[536.538309, "o", "**Step 2: Calculate standard deduction**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.538366, "o", "Per §152(c)(2)(A), the basic standard deduction for a joint return is 200% of the amount in §152(c)(2)(C), which is $3,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538378, "o", "> "]
[536.538409, "o", "Standard deduction = 200% × $3,000 = $6,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.538423, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538453, "o", "> "]
[536.538479, "o", "**Step 3: Calculate exemption phaseout**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.538504, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.538526, "o", "Per §151(d)(1), the exemption amount is $2,000 per exemption.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.53855, "o", "> "]
[536.538581, "o", "Alice and spouse each get one exemption: 2 × $2,000 = $4,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538605, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538645, "o", "> "]
[536.53867, "o", "Per §151(d)(3)(A) and §68(b)(A), the applicable amount for joint returns is $300,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538705, "o", "> "]
[536.538732, "o", "Alice's gross income is $684,642.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.538758, "o", "Excess AGI = $684,642 - $300,000 = $384,642\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.538785, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.538816, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.538859, "o", "Per §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage is 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538885, "o", "> "]
[536.538933, "o", "Number of $2,500 fractions = ceiling($384,642 / $2,500) = ceiling(153.8568) = 154\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.538959, "o", "> "]
[536.538986, "o", "Applicable percentage = 154 × 2% = 308%\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.539007, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539047, "o", "Per §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage cannot exceed 100%.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.539071, "o", "> "]
[536.539123, "o", "Therefore, exemption amount = $4,000 × 100% = $0 (fully phased out)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.53916, "o", "**Step 4: Calculate taxable income**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.539188, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.53922, "o", "Taxable income = Gross income - Standard deduction - Exemptions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.53923, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539272, "o", "Taxable income = $684,642 - $6,000 - $0 = $678,642\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.539307, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> **Step 5: Calculate tax**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.539336, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539371, "o", "Per §1(a)(v), since taxable income ($678,642) is over $250,000:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.539402, "o", "> "]
[536.53943, "o", "Tax = $75,528.50 + 39.6% × ($678,642 - $250,000)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[536.539457, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539486, "o", "Tax = $75,528.50 + 0.396 × $428,642\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539516, "o", "Tax = $75,528.50 + $169,742.23\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539547, "o", "Tax = $245,270.73\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[536.539573, "o", "> "]
[536.539587, "o", "Rounded to the nearest dollar: $245,271\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539723, "o", "The agricultural labor information (employees Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George) is not relevant to Alice's personal income tax calculation under these statutes.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[536.539756, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539787, "o", "## Answer\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Answer: 245271\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[536.539814, "o", "EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
