[1489.249637, "o", "245:§3301. Rate of tax\r\n251:§3306. Definitions\r\n"]
[1489.250057, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@9aaaffa9e76f:/app# "]
[1508.993469, "i", "sed -n '245,260p' /app/statute.txt\n"]
[1508.993882, "o", "sed -n '245,260p' /app/statute.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1508.995737, "o", "§3301. Rate of tax\r\n\r\nThere is hereby imposed on every employer (as defined in section 3306(a)) for each calendar year an excise tax, with respect to having individuals in his employ, equal to 6 percent of the total wages (as defined in section 3306(b)) paid by such employer during the calendar year with respect to employment (as defined in section 3306(c)).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n§3306. Definitions\r\n\r\n(a) Employer\r\n\r\n    (1) In general\r\n\r\n"]
[1508.995804, "o", "    The term \"employer\" means, with respect to any calendar year, any person who-\r\n\r\n        (A) during the calendar year or the preceding calendar year paid wages of $1,500 or more, or\r\n\r\n"]
[1508.996119, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@9aaaffa9e76f:/app# "]
[1509.495511, "i", "sed -n '260,280p' /app/statute.txt\n"]
[1509.495809, "o", "sed -n '260,280p' /app/statute.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1509.497576, "o", "\r\n        (B) on each of some 10 days during the calendar year or during the preceding calendar year, each day being in a different calendar week, employed at least one individual in employment for some portion of the day.\r\n\r\n    For purposes of this paragraph, there shall not be taken into account any wages paid to, or employment of, an employee performing domestic services referred to in paragraph (3).\r\n\r\n    (2) Agricultural labor\r\n\r\n    In the case of agricultural labor, the term \"employer\" means, with respect to any calendar year, any person who-\r\n\r\n        (A) during the calendar year or the preceding calendar year paid wages of $20,000 or more for agricultural labor, or\r\n\r\n        (B) on each of some 10 days during the calendar year or during the preceding calendar year, each day being in a different calendar week, employed at least 5 individuals in employment in agricultural labor for some portion of the day.\r\n\r\n    (3) Domestic service\r\n\r\n    In the case of domestic service in a private home, local c"]
[1509.497608, "o", "ollege club, or local chapter of a college fraternity or sorority, the term \"employer\" means, with respect to any calendar year, any person who during the calendar year or the preceding calendar year paid wages in cash of $1,000 or more for such service.\r\n\r\n    (4) Special rule\r\n\r\n    A person treated as an employer under paragraph (3) shall not be treated as an employer with respect to wages paid for any service other than domestic service referred to in paragraph (3) unless such person is treated as an employer under paragraph (1) or (2) with respect to such other service.\r\n\r\n"]
[1509.497826, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@9aaaffa9e76f:/app# "]
[1677.095706, "i", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\n## Statute\n\n**§1. Tax imposed** (lines 1-17)\n\n(a) Married individuals filing joint returns and surviving spouses\n\nThere is hereby imposed on the taxable income of-\n\n    (1) every married individual (as defined in section 7703) who makes a single return jointly with his spouse, and\n\n    (2) every surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\n\na tax determined in accordance with the following:\n\n    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $36,900;\n    (ii) $5,535, plus 28% of the excess over $36,900 if the taxable income is over $36,900 but not over $89,150;\n    (iii) $20,165, plus 31% of the excess over $89,150 if the taxable income is over $89,150 but not over $140,000;\n    (iv) $35,928.50, plus 36% of the excess over $140,000 if the taxable income is over $140,000 but not over $250,000;\n    (v) $75,528.50, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000.\n\n**§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions** (lines 5"]
[1677.095782, "i", "7-94)\n\n(d) Exemption amount\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\n\n    (3) Phaseout\n\n        (A) In general\n\n        In the case of any taxpayer whose adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b), the exemption amount shall be reduced by the applicable percentage.\n\n        (B) Applicable percentage\n\n        For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term \"applicable percentage\" means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting \"$1,250\" for \"$2,500\". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.\n\n**§152. Standard deduction** (lines 372-388)\n\n(c) Standard deduction\n\nFor purposes of this subtitle-\n\n    (2) Bas"]
[1677.095793, "i", "ic standard deduction\n\n    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\n\n        (A) 200 percent of the dollar amount in effect under subparagraph (C) for the taxable year in the case of-\n\n            (i) a joint return, or\n\n            (ii) a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\n\n        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\n\n        (C) $3,000 in any other case.\n\n**§68. Overall limitation on itemized deductions** (lines 475-494)\n\n(b) Applicable amount\n\n    (1) In general\n\n    For purposes of this section, the term \"applicable amount\" means-\n\n        (A) $300,000 in the case of a joint return or a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\n\n**§3301. Rate of tax** (lines 245-250)\n\nThere is hereby imposed on every employer (as defined in section 3306(a)) for each calendar year an excise tax, with respect to having individuals in his employ, equal to 6 percent of the total wages (as defined in section 3306(b)) paid by such employer duri"]
[1677.095797, "i", "ng the calendar year with respect to employment (as defined in section 3306(c)).\n\n**§3306. Definitions** (lines 251-329)\n\n(a) Employer\n\n    (2) Agricultural labor\n\n    In the case of agricultural labor, the term \"employer\" means, with respect to any calendar year, any person who-\n\n        (A) during the calendar year or the preceding calendar year paid wages of $20,000 or more for agricultural labor, or\n\n        (B) on each of some 10 days during the calendar year or during the preceding calendar year, each day being in a different calendar week, employed at least 5 individuals in employment in agricultural labor for some portion of the day.\n\n(b) Wages\n\nFor purposes of this chapter, the term \"wages\" means all remuneration for employment, including the cash value of all remuneration (including benefits) paid in any medium other than cash; except that such term shall not include-\n\n    (1) that part of the remuneration which, after remuneration (other than remuneration referred to in the succeeding paragraphs o"]
[1677.095812, "i", "f this subsection) equal to $7,000 with respect to employment has been paid to an individual by an employer during any calendar year, is paid to such individual by such employer during such calendar year;\n\n## Reasoning\n\n**Step 1: Determine filing status**\nAlice files a joint return with her spouse. Per §1(a), the tax brackets for \"Married individuals filing joint returns\" apply.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate income tax**\n\n**Step 2a: Standard deduction**\nPer §152(c)(2)(A), the basic standard deduction for a joint return is 200% of the amount in §152(c)(2)(C), which is $3,000.\nStandard deduction = 200% × $3,000 = $6,000\n\n**Step 2b: Exemption phaseout**\nPer §151(d)(1), the exemption amount is $2,000 per exemption.\nAlice and spouse each get one exemption: 2 × $2,000 = $4,000\n\nPer §151(d)(3)(A) and §68(b)(A), the applicable amount for joint returns is $300,000.\nAlice's gross income is $684,642.\n\nExcess AGI = $684,642 - $300,000 = $384,642\n\nPer §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage is 2 percentage points for eac"]
[1677.095816, "i", "h $2,500 (or fraction thereof).\nNumber of $2,500 fractions = ceiling($384,642 / $2,500) = ceiling(153.8568) = 154\nApplicable percentage = 154 × 2% = 308%\n\nPer §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage cannot exceed 100%.\nTherefore, exemption amount = $4,000 × 100% = $0 (fully phased out)\n\n**Step 2c: Taxable income**\nTaxable income = Gross income - Standard deduction - Exemptions\nTaxable income = $684,642 - $6,000 - $0 = $678,642\n\n**Step 2d: Tax calculation**\nPer §1(a)(v), since taxable income ($678,642) is over $250,000:\nIncome tax = $75,528.50 + 39.6% × ($678,642 - $250,000)\nIncome tax = $75,528.50 + 0.396 × $428,642\nIncome tax = $75,528.50 + $169,742.23\nIncome tax = $245,270.73\n\n**Step 3: Calculate employment tax for agricultural labor**\n\n**Step 3a: Determine if Alice is an employer**\nPer §3306(a)(2)(B), an agricultural labor employer is one who \"on each of some 10 days during the calendar year...employed at least 5 individuals in employment in agricultural labor.\"\n\nAlice's employment schedule:\n- Jan "]
[1677.095819, "i", "24: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred)\n- Mar 3: 5 workers\n- Mar 19: 5 workers\n- Apr 2: 5 workers\n- May 9: 5 workers\n- Oct 15: 5 workers\n- Nov 8: 5 workers\n- Nov 22: 5 workers\n- Dec 1: 5 workers\n- Dec 3: 5 workers\n\nAlice employed 5 workers on 10 different days, meeting the threshold in §3306(a)(2)(B).\n\n**Step 3b: Calculate total wages**\nPer §3306(b), wages mean all remuneration for employment.\nWorker counts from payment schedule:\n- Bob: 10 occasions\n- Cameron: 11 occasions\n- Dan: 9 occasions\n- Emily: 10 occasions\n- Fred: 9 occasions\n- George: 8 occasions\n\nTotal occasions = 10 + 11 + 9 + 10 + 9 + 8 = 57\nWage per occasion = $632\nTotal wages = 57 × $632 = $36,024\n\n**Step 3c: Calculate taxable wages**\nPer §3306(b)(1), wages exclude only remuneration AFTER $7,000 is paid to an individual.\nSince no worker earned more than $7,000 (max was Cameron with 11 × $632 = $6,952), all wages are taxable.\nTaxable wages = $36,024\n\n**Step 3d: Employment tax calculation**\nPer §3301, the excise tax is 6% of total wage"]
[1677.095824, "i", "s.\nEmployment tax = 6% × $36,024 = $2,161.44\n\n**Step 4: Total tax**\nTotal tax = Income tax + Employment tax\nTotal tax = $245,270.73 + $2,161.44 = $247,432.17\n\nRounded to the nearest dollar: $247,432\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 247432\nEOF\n"]
[1677.096078, "o", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Statute\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> **§1. Tax imposed** (lines 1-17)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
