[1677.097561, "o", "(d) Exemption amount\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\ro\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.097575, "o", "> "]
[1677.097587, "o", "    (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.097661, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.097742, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r0\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.097931, "o", "    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     (3) Phaseout\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (A) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.098194, "o", "        In the case of any taxpayer whose adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b), the exemption amount shall be reduced by the applicable percentage.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         (B) Applicable percentage\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.098847, "o", "        For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term \"applicable percentage\" means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting \"$1,250\" for \"$2,500\". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\ra\u001b[?2004h> **§152. Standard deduction** (lines 372-388)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rp\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.098897, "o", "(c) Standard deduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.098907, "o", " \u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.098938, "o", "For purposes of this subtitle-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\re"]
[1677.098967, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.098991, "o", "    (2) Basic standard deduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.098999, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099043, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099096, "o", "    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[1677.09912, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.09915, "o", "> "]
[1677.099249, "o", "        (A) 200 percent of the dollar amount in effect under subparagraph (C) for the taxable year in the case of-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.099272, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099297, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099323, "o", "            (i) a joint return, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099349, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099413, "o", "            (ii) a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.099439, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099463, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099542, "o", "        (B) $4,400 in the case of a head of household (as defined in section 2(b)), or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.09955, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099578, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099611, "o", "        (C) $3,000 in any other case.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099633, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099655, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099719, "o", "**§68. Overall limitation on itemized deductions** (lines 475-494)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.099741, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099766, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099792, "o", "(b) Applicable amount\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099815, "o", "-\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.09984, "o", "    (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.099864, "o", "-\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.099939, "o", "    For purposes of this section, the term \"applicable amount\" means-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.099965, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rW"]
[1677.099986, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.100108, "o", "        (A) $300,000 in the case of a joint return or a surviving spouse (as defined in section 2(a)),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.100133, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r3"]
[1677.100155, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.100188, "o", "**§3301. Rate of tax** (lines 245-250)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.10021, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.100235, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.100703, "o", "There is hereby imposed on every employer (as defined in section 3306(a)) for each calendar year an excise tax, with respect to having individuals in his employ, equal to 6 percent of the total wages (as defined in section 3306(b)) paid by such employer during the calendar year with respect to employment (as defined in section 3306(c)).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.100711, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r "]
[1677.100737, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.100759, "o", "> "]
[1677.100788, "o", "**§3306. Definitions** (lines 251-329)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.100809, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.100826, "o", "$\u001b[?2004h> (a) Employer\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.10086, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r$\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.100888, "o", "    (2) Agricultural labor\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.100911, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\rn"]
[1677.100938, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.101047, "o", "    In the case of agricultural labor, the term \"employer\" means, with respect to any calendar year, any person who-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.10107, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.101093, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.101164, "o", "        (A) during the calendar year or the preceding calendar year paid wages of $20,000 or more for agricultural labor, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.101187, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.101212, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.101373, "o", "        (B) on each of some 10 days during the calendar year or during the preceding calendar year, each day being in a different calendar week, employed at least 5 individuals in employment in agricultural labor for some portion of the day.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.101395, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.101419, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> (b) Wages\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.101441, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.101595, "o", "For purposes of this chapter, the term \"wages\" means all remuneration for employment, including the cash value of all remuneration (including benefits) paid in any medium other than cash; except that such term shall not include-\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.101619, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.101644, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.101867, "o", "    (1) that part of the remuneration which, after remuneration (other than remuneration referred to in the succeeding paragraphs of this subsection) equal to $7,000 with respect to employment has been paid to an individual by an employer during any calendar year, is paid to such individual by such employer during such calendar year;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.101891, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.101915, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ## Reasoning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.10194, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.101964, "o", "**Step 1: Determine filing status**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.101988, "o", "> "]
[1677.102058, "o", "Alice files a joint return with her spouse. Per §1(a), the tax brackets for \"Married individuals filing joint returns\" apply.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.102082, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102109, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102137, "o", "**Step 2: Calculate income tax**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102162, "o", "**Step 2a: Standard deduction**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102264, "o", "Per §152(c)(2)(A), the basic standard deduction for a joint return is 200% of the amount in §152(c)(2)(C), which is $3,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102288, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102312, "o", "Standard deduction = 200% × $3,000 = $6,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.102334, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102355, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102377, "o", "**Step 2b: Exemption phaseout**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.10242, "o", "Per §151(d)(1), the exemption amount is $2,000 per exemption.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102445, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102479, "o", "Alice and spouse each get one exemption: 2 × $2,000 = $4,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.102506, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102529, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102569, "o", "Per §151(d)(3)(A) and §68(b)(A), the applicable amount for joint returns is $300,000.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.102591, "o", "> "]
[1677.102614, "o", "Alice's gross income is $684,642.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102639, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102664, "o", "Excess AGI = $684,642 - $300,000 = $384,642\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.10269, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102712, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102787, "o", "Per §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage is 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.102809, "o", "> "]
[1677.102861, "o", "Number of $2,500 fractions = ceiling($384,642 / $2,500) = ceiling(153.8568) = 154\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.102881, "o", "> "]
[1677.102905, "o", "Applicable percentage = 154 × 2% = 308%\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.102928, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.102947, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.102978, "o", "Per §151(d)(3)(B), the applicable percentage cannot exceed 100%.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103001, "o", "> "]
[1677.103043, "o", "Therefore, exemption amount = $4,000 × 100% = $0 (fully phased out)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.103061, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.103086, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.103106, "o", "**Step 2c: Taxable income**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.103149, "o", "Taxable income = Gross income - Standard deduction - Exemptions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.1032, "o", "Taxable income = $684,642 - $6,000 - $0 = $678,642\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103226, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.103247, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> **Step 2d: Tax calculation**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.10327, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.103304, "o", "Per §1(a)(v), since taxable income ($678,642) is over $250,000:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103312, "o", "> "]
[1677.103359, "o", "Income tax = $75,528.50 + 39.6% × ($678,642 - $250,000)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103383, "o", "> "]
[1677.103403, "o", "Income tax = $75,528.50 + 0.396 × $428,642\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103428, "o", "> "]
[1677.103455, "o", "Income tax = $75,528.50 + $169,742.23\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103477, "o", "> "]
[1677.103499, "o", "Income tax = $245,270.73\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103523, "o", "> "]
[1677.103549, "o", "**Step 3: Calculate employment tax for agricultural labor**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.103572, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.103599, "o", "**Step 3a: Determine if Alice is an employer**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103621, "o", "> "]
[1677.103748, "o", "Per §3306(a)(2)(B), an agricultural labor employer is one who \"on each of some 10 days during the calendar year...employed at least 5 individuals in employment in agricultural labor.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103755, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.103785, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.10381, "o", "> Alice's employment schedule:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.103835, "o", "> "]
[1677.103858, "o", "- Jan 24: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.103886, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.103928, "o", "- Mar 3: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Mar 19: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Apr 2: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.103963, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> - May 9: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.103983, "o", "- Oct 15: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104001, "o", "- Nov 8: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.104017, "o", "> "]
[1677.104026, "o", "- Nov 22: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.104045, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104281, "o", "- Dec 1: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104314, "o", "- Dec 3: 5 workers\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104338, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104383, "o", "Alice employed 5 workers on 10 different days, meeting the threshold in §3306(a)(2)(B).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.104408, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.10443, "o", "**Step 3b: Calculate total wages**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.10445, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104486, "o", "Per §3306(b), wages mean all remuneration for employment.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.104505, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104524, "o", "Worker counts from payment schedule:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.104541, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.10456, "o", "- Bob: 10 occasions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.10458, "o", "- Cameron: 11 occasions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.104599, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104621, "o", "- Dan: 9 occasions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.104641, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104661, "o", "- Emily: 10 occasions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Fred: 9 occasions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.104681, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104702, "o", "- George: 8 occasions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.104723, "o", "> "]
[1677.104748, "o", "Total occasions = 10 + 11 + 9 + 10 + 9 + 8 = 57\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.104782, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> Wage per occasion = $632\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104815, "o", "Total wages = 57 × $632 = $36,024\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.104836, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.104867, "o", "**Step 3c: Calculate taxable wages**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.104888, "o", "> "]
[1677.104942, "o", "Per §3306(b)(1), wages exclude only remuneration AFTER $7,000 is paid to an individual.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.104962, "o", "> "]
[1677.105036, "o", "Since no worker earned more than $7,000 (max was Cameron with 11 × $632 = $6,952), all wages are taxable.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105059, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105074, "o", "Taxable wages = $36,024\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.10509, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105107, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105128, "o", "**Step 3d: Employment tax calculation**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105147, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105175, "o", "Per §3301, the excise tax is 6% of total wages.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105195, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105219, "o", "Employment tax = 6% × $36,024 = $2,161.44\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.105236, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105253, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105274, "o", "**Step 4: Total tax**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105298, "o", "Total tax = Income tax + Employment tax\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105317, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105347, "o", "Total tax = $245,270.73 + $2,161.44 = $247,432.17\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1677.105366, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105386, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105405, "o", "Rounded to the nearest dollar: $247,432\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105425, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ## Answer\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105446, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> Answer: 247432\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.105465, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1677.105485, "o", "EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1677.107178, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@9aaaffa9e76f:/app# "]
